| `tests.isolation.tiers.<tier>.stores` | string | `temp` for every tier | a tier marker name mapped to `temp` or `any`: a closed set | `tests/isolation_guard.py` (`load_policy`), installed by `tests/conftest.py` | Sets where a test of the tier may open a sqlite database: `temp` allows one only under the roots `tests.isolation.tiers.<tier>.writes` names, and refuses a store `tests.isolation.stores` lists in any mode, reading included; a name that starts `file:` is judged both as a URI and as a file of that name in the working directory, because the audit event does not say which sqlite reads; `any` allows every database. A test with no marker this block names gets `temp`. | naming the live stores: `tests.isolation.stores` | always |
